    {
      "block_id": "2605.22715_p5_b88",
      "text": "Full-Body IMU Tokenization. Pre-training produces continuous, setup-stable sequence latents,\nwhile the motion-language model requires compact discrete inputs. As motivated in Section 1, feeding\nraw IMU streams into an LLM is inefficient. To connect wearable motion with language models, we\ntrain a full-body IMU tokenizer that discretizes the frozen graph encoder latent into compact IMU\ntokens, following recent motion-language tokenizers based on product quantization [23].\n",
      "bbox": [
        107.64,
        615.52,
        505.25,
        669.29
      ],
